  "components": [
    {
      "name": "Setting Key",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "setting-key",
      "description": "A signal setting with its name inside, its value below and the cable readback under it.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-key\"><span class=\"ds-key-label\">Range<i class=\"ds-dot\"></i></span><span class=\"ds-key-value\">Limited (64-940)</span><span class=\"ds-key-wire\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 12 12\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\"><path d=\"M2.2 6.4 4.8 9 9.8 3.2\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.9\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/></svg>Limited on the cable</span></div>",
      "css": ".ds-key{display:grid;gap:2px;width:220px;padding:9px 6px 9px 14px;border-radius:16px;background:var(--meso-key,#1f1f23);font-family:var(--meso, 'PGen Mesopic', 'Avenir Next', 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;transition:box-shadow .14s ease-out}.ds-key:hover{background:var(--meso-key-hi,#38383f);box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1.5px var(--accent,#8fe0d1)}.ds-key:focus-within{box-shadow:0 0 0 2px var(--focus-ring,#e9fffa)}.ds-key-label{font-size:.8125rem;font-weight:500;line-height:1.3;color:var(--text-muted,#8f8f96)}.ds-dot{display:inline-block;width:6px;height:6px;margin-left:7px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--accent,#8fe0d1);vertical-align:.12em}.ds-key-value{font-size:1rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--meso-lit,#e4e4e8)}.ds-key-wire{display:flex;gap:5px;align-items:center;font-size:.8125rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--text-secondary,#a2a2a8)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Setting Key, cable differs",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "setting-key",
      "description": "The cable carries something else than the setting: amber ring, triangle and text.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-key-d\"><span class=\"ds-kd-label\">Bit Depth</span><span class=\"ds-kd-value\">12-bit</span><span class=\"ds-kd-wire\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 12 12\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\"><path d=\"M6 1.2 11 10.4H1Z\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/></svg>10-bit on the cable</span></div>",
      "css": ".ds-key-d{display:grid;gap:2px;width:220px;padding:9px 6px 9px 14px;border-radius:16px;background:var(--meso-key,#1f1f23);box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1.5px var(--warning-text,#e8a55b);font-family:var(--meso, 'PGen Mesopic', 'Avenir Next', 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-kd-label{font-size:.8125rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--text-muted,#8f8f96)}.ds-kd-value{font-size:1rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--meso-lit,#e4e4e8)}.ds-kd-wire{display:flex;gap:5px;align-items:center;font-size:.8125rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--warning-text,#e8a55b)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Primary Button",
      "kind": "button",
      "refersTo": "button-primary",
      "description": "The one filled action, e.g. Apply.",
      "html": "<button class=\"ds-btn-primary\">Apply</button>",
      "css": ".ds-btn-primary{height:36px;padding:0 18px;border:0;border-radius:999px;background:var(--accent-fill,#6fcfbd);color:var(--on-accent,#05241f);font-family:var(--meso, 'PGen Mesopic', 'Avenir Next', 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif);font-weight:700;font-size:.875rem;cursor:pointer;transition:transform .14s ease-out}.ds-btn-primary:hover{background:var(--accent-fill2,#8adfce)}.ds-btn-primary:focus-visible{outline:0;box-shadow:0 0 0 2px var(--focus-ring,#e9fffa)}.ds-btn-primary:active{transform:scale(.97)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Quiet Button",
      "kind": "button",
      "refersTo": "button-quiet",
      "description": "A card reset: transparent until hovered, amber on hover because it undoes work.",
      "html": "<button class=\"ds-btn-quiet\">Reset Defaults</button>",
      "css": ".ds-btn-quiet{height:32px;padding:0 14px;border:0;border-radius:999px;background:transparent;color:var(--text-secondary,#a2a2a8);font-family:var(--meso, 'PGen Mesopic', 'Avenir Next', 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif);font-weight:700;font-size:.8125rem;cursor:pointer}.ds-btn-quiet:hover,.ds-btn-quiet:focus-visible{background:var(--neutral-fill,#2b2b31);color:var(--warning-text,#e8a55b);outline:0}.ds-btn-quiet:active{transform:scale(.97)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Rail Navigation",
      "kind": "nav",
      "refersTo": "nav-item-current",
      "description": "Desktop workspace rail: the current item lit on the panel tone with an aqua icon.",
      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-rail\"><a class=\"ds-rail-item\" aria-current=\"page\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" width=\"19\" height=\"19\"><rect x=\"2.5\" y=\"4\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><path d=\"M7 17h6\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/></svg>Output</a><a class=\"ds-rail-item\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" width=\"19\" height=\"19\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1.5\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><rect x=\"11\" y=\"11\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" rx=\"1.5\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/></svg>Patterns</a></nav>",
      "css": ".ds-rail{display:grid;gap:2px;width:212px;padding:8px;background:var(--surface-sidebar,#0a0a0c);font-family:var(--meso, 'PGen Mesopic', 'Avenir Next', 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif)}.ds-rail-item{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;min-height:42px;padding:9px 14px;border-radius:14px;font-size:.9375rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--text-secondary,#a2a2a8);cursor:pointer}.ds-rail-item:hover{background:var(--hover-bg,rgba(255,255,255,.06))}.ds-rail-item[aria-current=page]{background:var(--surface-card,#141416);color:var(--meso-lit,#e4e4e8);font-weight:700}.ds-rail-item[aria-current=page] svg{color:var(--accent,#8fe0d1)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Status Readout",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "status-readout",
      "description": "The header capsule: the signal leads, a hairline, then the chain behind it.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-readout\"><span class=\"ds-ro-sig\"><i class=\"ds-ro-dot\"></i>Signal <b>HDR10 3840x2160 10-bit</b></span><span><i class=\"ds-ro-dot\"></i>Pi Connected</span><span>52 °C</span></div>",
      "css": ".ds-readout{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:16px;min-height:36px;padding:4px 18px;border-radius:18px;background:var(--surface-card,#141416);font-family:var(--meso, 'PGen Mesopic', 'Avenir Next', 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif);font-size:.8125rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--text-secondary,#a2a2a8);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-ro-sig{padding-right:16px;box-shadow:1px 0 0 var(--border,#2b2b30)}.ds-ro-sig b{margin-left:4px;font-size:.9375rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--meso-lit,#e4e4e8)}.ds-ro-dot{display:inline-block;width:7px;height:7px;margin-right:7px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--status-success,#5fb878)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Card",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "card",
      "description": "One soft panel per section, no border, title in the headline size.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-card\"><h2>Signal Self-Test</h2><p>Draws known codes in twelve signal modes and reads the pixels back.</p></section>",
      "css": ".ds-card{width:320px;padding:22px 24px 24px;border-radius:22px;background:var(--surface-card,#141416);font-family:var(--meso, 'PGen Mesopic', 'Avenir Next', 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif);color:var(--text-secondary,#a2a2a8)}.ds-card h2{margin:0 0 18px;font-size:1.1875rem;font-weight:700;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-.01em;color:var(--meso-lit,#e4e4e8)}.ds-card p{margin:0;font-size:.875rem;line-height:1.45}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Note Well",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "note-well",
      "description": "What is read, not pressed: a note or a verdict sunk one tone below the card.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-well\">No meter connected. Plug in a colorimeter over USB.</div>",
      "css": ".ds-well{width:300px;padding:12px 14px;border-radius:16px;background:var(--meso-well,#0d0d0f);font-family:var(--meso, 'PGen Mesopic', 'Avenir Next', 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif);font-size:.8125rem;line-height:1.4;color:var(--text-secondary,#a2a2a8)}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Mesopic",
    "overview": "Mesopic vision is what the eye does between daylight and darkness, and that is\nwhere a calibrator works: in a dimmed room, the display under test the\nbrightest thing in it, the phone or laptop held at arm's length. The interface\nlives in that light. It is dark by default, low in chrome contrast, and lets\nthe picture on the TV be the only bright object. Hierarchy comes from tone\nsteps, not outlines: a well for what is read, a key for what is pressed, a lit\nkey for what is chosen.\n\nThe face is round and geometric (Gabarito, served by the Pi itself as\n\"PGen Mesopic\", OFL 1.1), set bold for what the calibrator reads and medium\nfor labels, with tabular figures everywhere so codes and clocks never jitter.\nControls are soft keys and pills with their name inside. One pale aqua accent\nmarks what is current, chosen or about to be applied; amber, coral and green\nare reserved for state.\n\nThe look is modern and bold, not technical. The rejected first redesign\n(\"Service Manual\") showed what this system is not: no monospace or typewriter\nfaces for UI text, no stencil or lettering faces, nothing retro or\nmanual-like.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Dark default that does not light the room; a working light theme in the same grammar.",
      "Tone steps instead of 1 px frames: well, key, lit key.",
      "One accent, used for current, chosen and pending; hue never carries state alone.",
      "Bold round type with tabular figures; nothing under 12 px.",
      "Calibration colour is data: nothing tints, blends or lies over it."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Voice Rule",
        "body": "Aqua is the only accent. It marks current, chosen or pending, never decoration.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Data Colour Rule",
        "body": "A calibration colour (swatch, preview, chart patch) is shown exactly: no tint, filter, blend, opacity, gradient or translucent layer over it.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Palette Override Rule",
        "body": "The Mesopic tokens apply only without `data-palette`. The other themes (Volt, Natrium, OLED …) set their own colours and inherit the Mesopic shapes, type and tone grammar.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No-Mono Rule",
        "body": "No monospace, typewriter, stencil or lettering face for UI text. Hex dumps in the infoframe decoder are the one place a monospace stack remains.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Rule",
        "body": "Every number uses tabular figures, so a changing code or clock never shifts its neighbours.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tone-Step Rule",
        "body": "A boundary is a change of tone, not a 1 px line. What is live or chosen among peers carries a 1.5 px inset ring (aqua, or amber when the cable differs).",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** build boundaries from the four tone steps (well, key, lit key, panel) before reaching for a line.",
      "**Do** keep aqua for current, chosen and pending; use amber only for a cable difference or a destructive hover.",
      "**Do** pair every state hue with a word or a mark, and keep forced-colours rules for new marks.",
      "**Do** start new lines on the 24 px edge and keep text at 12 px or more.",
      "**Do** put long explanations behind a help mark, and show what the cable carries in the field it concerns."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use monospace, typewriter, stencil or lettering faces for UI text, or anything retro or manual-like (the rejected \"Service Manual\" direction).",
      "**Don't** draw 1 px frames around tiles, tabs or panels.",
      "**Don't** add a second accent colour or a gradient to the chrome.",
      "**Don't** tint, blend, filter or overlay a calibration colour, and don't put a translucent layer or drop shadow where swatches scroll under it.",
      "**Don't** load fonts or scripts from the internet; the Pi serves everything itself."
    ]
  }
}